<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Secret society</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as secret societies</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A secret society is an organisation whose membership, rituals or knowledge are restricted to initiates. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luba-empire">Luba Empire</a> the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bambudye">Bambudye</a> society acted as custodian of historical memory and as a check on royal excess. The Luba Empire and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lunda-empire">Lunda Empire</a> profiles both show such societies playing a significant role in governance and political legitimacy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/secret-society.jpg" alt="Secret society" width="320" height="244" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Miss Alice Donlevy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Secret_Society_Buildings_New_Haven.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
